---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';

const path = '/terms/';
const updated = '21 August 2026';
---

<Base
  title="Terms of Use | Next Scale Digital"
  description="Terms covering the use of the Next Scale Digital website, including what the free audit is and is not, and how client engagements are governed."
  path={path}
  breadcrumbs={[{ name: 'Home', href: '/' }, { name: 'Terms', href: path }]}
>
  <section class="legal-hero">
    <div class="wrap-tight">
      <span class="eyebrow">Legal</span>
      <h1>Terms of use</h1>
      <p class="legal-date">Last updated {updated}</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap-tight legal">
      <h2>What these cover</h2>
      <p>
        These terms cover your use of nextscaledigital.com. They do not govern client
        work. Every engagement runs under its own written agreement, and where that
        agreement and this page disagree, the agreement wins.
      </p>

      <h2>The content on this site</h2>
      <p>
        The articles and service pages here are general information about search
        marketing. They are written from work done for businesses in the Greater
        Toronto Area and they may not apply to your situation. Nothing on this site
        is a guarantee of a search ranking, a lead volume or a revenue outcome.
      </p>
      <p>
        Search engines change how they rank, competitors change what they do, and
        neither is under our control or anyone else&rsquo;s. Treat any figure on this site
        as a description of the past rather than a forecast.
      </p>

      <h2>The free audit</h2>
      <p>
        The audit offered on the contact page is free and carries no obligation on
        either side. Requesting one does not create a client relationship, and we may
        decline to run one where the business is outside what we can usefully help with.
      </p>
      <p>
        The report is provided as-is, based on data available at the time it is run.
        Ranking and search volume data comes from third-party sources and from Google&rsquo;s
        own tools, and can change day to day. You are free to use the report however you
        like, including taking it to another agency.
      </p>

      <h2>Ownership</h2>
      <p>
        The text, design and code of this site belong to {site.legalName}. Client names
        and marks appearing on it belong to those clients and are used to describe work
        we performed.
      </p>
      <p>
        You may quote from the articles with attribution and a link. You may not
        republish a page in full.
      </p>

      <h2>Links out</h2>
      <p>
        Where this site links to somewhere else, we do not control what is on the other
        end and are not responsible for it.
      </p>

      <h2>Liability</h2>
      <p>
        This site is provided without warranty. To the extent the law allows,
        {site.legalName} is not liable for loss arising from use of, or reliance on,
        information published here. Client engagements carry their own liability terms,
        agreed in writing.
      </p>

      <h2>Governing law</h2>
      <p>
        These terms are governed by the laws of the Province of Ontario and the federal
        laws of Canada that apply in it.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions go to <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .legal-hero { background: var(--ink); color: var(--fg-on-ink); padding-block: var(--sp-7); }
  .legal-hero .eyebrow { color: var(--brand-lite); }
  .legal-hero .eyebrow::after { background: var(--rule-dark); }
  .legal-hero h1 { color: var(--paper); font-size: var(--step-3); margin-bottom: var(--sp-3); }
  .legal-date { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.76rem; color: var(--fg-faint); margin: 0; }

  .legal h2 { font-size: var(--step-1); margin-top: var(--sp-7); margin-bottom: var(--sp-3); }
  .legal h2:first-child { margin-top: 0; }
  .legal p { margin-bottom: var(--sp-4); }
</style>
